model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Request reliability counts only the retained local model and gateway sources. Explicit purpose records match the exact pool, source and hashed client key; unclassified keys count as real. Proof counts remain visible separately, while token and cost totals retain every request. The same SQL read supplies the overview and rolling five-minute, one-hour and twenty-four-hour request windows. Empty real traffic has no success rate. Optional reliability reads use a savepoint so an unavailable monitor cannot discard the usage, token or cost answers. Availability RPC failure retains an independently measured reliability verdict and both closed failure classes. An inactive, stale, lagging or unclassified capture cannot establish the objective. The once-per-minute availability check-in reports only the synthetic pool probe. Real-request success below 99 percent emits its own error through the existing observability route. Missing collection remains unknown in the interface and emits a separate reliability incident with bounded counts and a closed reason. It never becomes an availability outage. Recent real failures emit their own signal even when the longer success objective is met. Empty real traffic and proof-only failures do not report an outage. Before dispatch, the Worker assigns a request identity and records metadata-only start and terminal evidence. Home usage remains append only. Video job status remains separate from successful HTTP receipt or poll delivery. Terminal failure overlays the final matching Home attempt; finished requests awaiting Home collection count once and disappear from that fallback when usage arrives. Missing terminal tables or abandoned starts cannot establish a green objective. Counts and closed reasons leave the service; keys and request content do not."
      constraint "Release provisioning applies the additive named traffic-purpose schema through the shared model-history migrator before Worker activation. Migration failure blocks activation; the private reviewed schema operation uses the same runner. It never rewrites request history. Purpose changes use the private operations entrypoint with a dry run listing exact retained request identifiers, current classifications and an evidence hash. Applying requires the digest of that selection; a changed selection refuses. A started local receipt prevents replay after an unknown apply outcome. Restoring a proof key to real uses the same reviewed path. Public app and model routes cannot change purpose."
    }
  }
  basalt.telemetry -[sync]-> basalt.pool "read request reliability contracts for monitor diagnostics"
}
